David Ernst

Usage:
    content-census-bi [options] <reportPath>...
Arguments:
    <reportPath>    A census report (audio*.csv, video*.csv, images*.csv,
                    books*.csv, comics*.csv, or the .tsv of each), or a folder to
                    look for them in, recursively. Several may be given,
                    including several libraries' worth of the same type: they are
                    loaded into one cube per type and stay separable along its
                    "library" axis.
Options:
    (may be given before the reports or after them)
    -o, --database <file>
                    Write the database to <file> instead of to
                    contentCensusBI.duckdb beside the first report. The .html page
                    is always written beside it, under the same name.
    -e, --export-dir <dir>
                    Also export each cube as <type>Cube.csv into <dir>.
    -c, --query <sql>
                    Run one query against the finished database and print it.
                    The tables are named above; try
                      -c "SELECT * FROM videoCube WHERE depth = 1 AND resolution != 'ALL'"
    -s, --show-totals
                    Print each cube's grand total when it is built.
    -h, --help      Print this help page.
    -v, --verbose   Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                    failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                    lines.
    -q, --quiet     Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
